---
title: "Automotive · TISAX & continuous validation | VORNAC"
description: "Continuous penetration testing for automotive OEMs and suppliers. TISAX-aligned validation plus adversarial testing of connected vehicles, APIs, and binaries."
i18nKey: industries-automotive
ogType: website
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block extraHead %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/industries.css">
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Service",
      "@id": "{{ pageUrls['industries-automotive'] | absoluteUrl(site.domain) }}#service",
      "name": "Security validation for automotive supply chains",
      "serviceType": "Penetration Testing for Automotive",
      "description": "Continuous penetration testing for automotive OEMs and suppliers. TISAX-aligned validation plus adversarial testing of connected vehicles, APIs, and binaries.",
      "provider": { "@id": "https://www.vornac.com/#organization" },
      "areaServed": [
        { "@type": "Country", "name": "Germany" },
        { "@type": "Country", "name": "Austria" },
        { "@type": "Country", "name": "Switzerland" },
        { "@type": "Place", "name": "European Union" }
      ],
      "audience": {
        "@type": "BusinessAudience",
        "audienceType": "Automotive OEMs and Tier-N suppliers in the European automotive supply chain"
      },
      "category": "Cybersecurity / Automotive",
      "url": "{{ pageUrls['industries-automotive'] | absoluteUrl(site.domain) }}",
      "about": [
        { "@type": "Thing", "name": "TISAX assessment" },
        { "@type": "Thing", "name": "VDA ISA" },
        { "@type": "Thing", "name": "Connected vehicle security" },
        { "@type": "Thing", "name": "ECU and firmware testing" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "{{ pageUrls.index | absoluteUrl(site.domain) }}" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Industries", "item": "{{ pageUrls['industries'] | absoluteUrl(site.domain) }}" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Automotive", "item": "{{ pageUrls['industries-automotive'] | absoluteUrl(site.domain) }}" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
</script>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<main class="ind-page">
    <section class="ind-hero">
        <div class="ind-hero-inner">
            <p class="ind-hero-breadcrumb"><a href="{{ pageUrls.industries }}">Industries</a> / Automotive</p>
            <span class="ind-hero-framework">TISAX</span>
            <h1 class="ind-hero-headline">Security validation for <span class="ind-hero-headline-emph">automotive supply chains</span></h1>
            <p class="ind-hero-sub">OEMs and Tier suppliers must satisfy TISAX and customer audit programs while shipping connected software faster. VORNAC adds continuous, exploit-proven adversarial validation across web, APIs, binaries, and cloud, with evidence your assessors can verify.</p>
            <div class="ind-hero-actions">
                {% include "partials/hero-demo-button.njk" %}
                <a href="{{ pageUrls.pentesting }}#coverage" class="ind-btn-ghost">See coverage</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ind-section ind-section--cream">
        <div class="ind-section-inner">
            <header class="ind-section-head">
                <h2 class="ind-section-title">What TISAX and OEM programs require</h2>
                <p class="ind-section-lead">Information security assessment for the automotive industry, plus customer-specific requirements on connected products.</p>
            </header>
            <div class="ind-req-grid">
                <article class="ind-req-card"><h3 class="ind-req-card-title">TISAX assessment objectives</h3><p class="ind-req-card-desc">Protection levels aligned with VDA ISA: prototype protection, data protection, and connection to third parties.</p></article>
                <article class="ind-req-card"><h3 class="ind-req-card-title">Connected vehicle &amp; backend</h3><p class="ind-req-card-desc">Telematics, OTA updates, mobile apps, and API backends. Real attack paths, not checkbox scans.</p></article>
                <article class="ind-req-card"><h3 class="ind-req-card-title">Binary &amp; embedded software</h3><p class="ind-req-card-desc">.exe, .dmg, firmware, and ECU-related deliverables. Reverse engineering and exploit validation where applicable.</p></article>
                <article class="ind-req-card"><h3 class="ind-req-card-title">Supplier cascade</h3><p class="ind-req-card-desc">Tier-N suppliers must prove the same rigor as OEMs. Continuous evidence beats annual assessment snapshots.</p></article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ind-gap-band">
        <div class="ind-gap-inner">
            <div>
                <h2 class="ind-gap-title">TISAX every three years is not enough</h2>
                <p class="ind-gap-text">New vehicle lines, supplier integrations, and OTA releases change your exposure between assessments. Continuous validation keeps your label and your customers&rsquo; trust.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ind-gap-stat">
                <div class="ind-gap-stat-num">2–5h</div>
                <p class="ind-gap-stat-label">From trigger to actionable finding, on every release.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ind-section ind-section--dark">
        <div class="ind-section-inner">
            <header class="ind-section-head ind-section-head--light"><h2 class="ind-section-title">How VORNAC helps automotive</h2></header>
            <ul class="ind-help-list">
                <li class="ind-help-item"><span class="ind-help-num">1</span><div><h3 class="ind-help-title">TISAX-mapped reporting</h3><p class="ind-help-desc">Findings aligned to assessment objectives and control expectations. Ready for ENX and customer audits.</p></div></li>
                <li class="ind-help-item"><span class="ind-help-num">2</span><div><h3 class="ind-help-title">Full-stack coverage</h3><p class="ind-help-desc">External surface, cloud, APIs, binaries (.exe, .dmg, .apk). One platform, one evidence trail.</p></div></li>
                <li class="ind-help-item"><span class="ind-help-num">3</span><div><h3 class="ind-help-title">Hosted and operated in Germany</h3><p class="ind-help-desc">No US-jurisdiction tooling for prototype and production data. German data centres run by German providers, built for European automotive supply chains.</p></div></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ind-related">
        <div class="ind-related-inner">
            <p class="ind-related-title">Also relevant</p>
            <div class="ind-related-links">
                <a href="{{ pageUrls['industries-enterprise'] }}" class="ind-related-link">Enterprise (NIS2)</a>
                <a href="{{ pageUrls['industries-critical-infrastructure'] }}" class="ind-related-link">Critical infrastructure</a>
                <a href="{{ pageUrls.pentesting }}" class="ind-related-link">VORNAC Pentesting</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ind-cta">
        <div class="ind-cta-inner">
            <h2 class="ind-cta-headline">Keep TISAX evidence <em>current</em> between assessments.</h2>
            <div class="ind-cta-actions">
                {% include "partials/hero-demo-button.njk" %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
{% endblock %}
